      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Levels of Organization in the Human Body"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The chapter outlines the foundational levels of organization in the human biological structure.",
        "Key processing and transport networks include the Digestive, Respiratory, Circulatory, and Excretory systems.",
        "Control and integration of bodily functions are managed by the Nervous and Endocrine systems.",
        "Structural support, movement, and continuation of life are governed by the Skeletal, Muscular, and Reproductive systems."
      ],
